{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     media — one responsive image. EVERY image on the site goes through here.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     That is the point: this is the only place `loading`, `decoding`, `srcset`
     and `sizes` are decided, so they cannot be right in five templates and
     wrong in the sixth.

     PARAMETERS
       src         the image (required)
       alt         alternative text; pass "" for a decorative image whose link
                   is already labelled
       sizes       defaults to full-viewport, which is right for a hero and
                   wrong for a card — cards pass their own
       eager       truthy → load immediately, no reveal
       decorative  truthy → aria-hidden

     ── Lazy, but NOT the first image ──────────────────────────────────────
     `loading="lazy"` on an image already in the viewport DELAYS it: the
     browser must lay the page out before it knows the image is visible, so
     the request starts later than an eager one would. On a hero that is a
     direct hit to Largest Contentful Paint — the one metric a theme is judged
     on. Hence `eager`, and hence heroes passing it.

     ── The reveal ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     `.ns-reveal` is NSDS's clip-reveal; type-fx.js observes it and sets
     [data-fx-in] on entry, so this needs no theme JavaScript. It is safe
     rather than decorative-at-the-cost-of-content because the hidden start
     state lives inside `@media (scripting: enabled)` — with JS off the image
     is simply there — and the animation's FINAL state is the correct one, so
     prefers-reduced-motion leaves it visible rather than invisible.

     An eager image skips the wrapper: revealing the hero means hiding the
     largest thing on the page until a script runs.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
{{#if src}}
    {{#if eager}}
        <img srcset="{{img_url src size="s"}} 300w,
                     {{img_url src size="m"}} 600w,
                     {{img_url src size="l"}} 1000w,
                     {{img_url src size="xl"}} 2000w"
             sizes="{{#if sizes}}{{sizes}}{{else}}100vw{{/if}}"
             src="{{img_url src size="l"}}"
             alt="{{alt}}" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"
             {{#if decorative}}aria-hidden="true"{{/if}}>
    {{else}}
        <span class="ns-reveal"><span>
            <img srcset="{{img_url src size="s"}} 300w,
                         {{img_url src size="m"}} 600w,
                         {{img_url src size="l"}} 1000w"
                 sizes="{{#if sizes}}{{sizes}}{{else}}100vw{{/if}}"
                 src="{{img_url src size="m"}}"
                 alt="{{alt}}" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                 {{#if decorative}}aria-hidden="true"{{/if}}>
        </span></span>
    {{/if}}
{{/if}}
